{{Quote|Don't worry. ''We're'' defective too.|Omega, to Gonky|<ref name="Rescue" />}}
'''Gonky''' was a defective<ref name="Rescue" /> [[GNK-series power droid]], who served [[Clone Force 99]] aboard the [[Marauder (Omicron-class)|''Marauder'']].<ref name="Databank" /> [[Wrecker]] frequently used the [[droid]] as a weightlifting aid.<ref name="Cut and Run EG">{{SW|url=series/the-bad-batch/cut-and-run-episode-guide|text="Cut and Run" Episode Guide &#124; The Bad Batch}}</ref> As a defective unit, Gonky's power unit could not fully charge. The [[Cloning|enhanced clone]] [[Omega]] used the droid as a cot for a brief time.<ref name="Replacements">{{TBB|Replacements}}</ref> Additionally, she spoke to Gonky on occasion, showing him her [[Clone trooper doll|trooper doll]]. When the ''Marauder'' was boarded by enemy [[Zygerrian]]s, Omega told the droid to hide, though he simply powered down.<ref name="Rampage">{{TBB|Rampage (episode)}}</ref>

Omega tried to fix Gonky's power unit to allow him to charge fully, but [[Hunter]] told her it was no use since he was a defective unit. The young clone comforted Gonky by saying that they were all [[Genetically defective clone|defective]]. During the Bad Batch's [[Extraction on Daro|mission]] to [[Daro]], Gonky provided extra power to the ship when it was attacked by Imperial [[Alpha-3 Nimbus-class V-wing starfighter|V-wing starfighters]], but when a second group of V-wings opened fire, Gonky short circuited.<ref name="War-Mantle">{{TBB|War-Mantle}}</ref>

During a [[Mission to Cid's mine|mission]] to [[Ciddarin Scaleback]]'s [[Cid's mine|mine]] on [[Ipsidon]], the ''Marauder'' got stolen by a [[thief]] and [[miner]] named [[Benni Baro]], who had disabled the ship's transponder, to prevent the Bad Batch from tracking it.<ref name="The Crossing">{{TBB|The Crossing}}</ref> But since Gonky was left aboard the ''Marauder'', the Batch was able to track him, in order to [[Mokkotown Liberation|reclaim them at]] [[Mokkotown]].<ref name="Retrieval">{{TBB|Retrieval (episode)}}</ref>

A while later after being through many events with the Bad Batch, Gonky was on [[Pabu]] as the group prepared to leave the island. He was with Wrecker while he was loading supplies, and was saved from destruction by Wrecker when [[CX-2]] blew the ''Marauder'' to pieces in order to keep the Batch from leaving.<ref name="Point of No Return">{{TBB|Point of No Return (The Bad Batch)}}</ref>

When Omega eventually left Pabu in [[Omega's ship|her ship]] to join the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], Gonky accompanied her.<ref name="Cavalry">{{TBB|The Cavalry Has Arrived}}</ref>

{{Droid-stub}}

==Skills and abilities==
Gonky was capable of serving as a table for his squadmates to play board games on.<ref name="War-Mantle">{{TBB|War-Mantle}}</ref> Wrecker was also known to use Gonky as exercise equipment.<ref name="Databank" />

==Behind the scenes==
Gonky first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' episode "[[A Distant Echo]]," albeit unnamed.<ref name="Cut and Run EG" /><ref name="DistantEcho">{{TCW|A Distant Echo}}</ref> He was later identified on the [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]].<ref name="Databank" /> In the [[Canon|non-canon]] ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga]]'', Gonky appears in the mission "Gonk with the Hyperwind," where the player escorts him to a [[Power socket|battery slot]] in [[Pau City]] while protecting him from [[B1-series battle droid]]s.<ref name="LEGO">''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga]]''</ref>

